Z||000003||Carrolles||09-28-1999||07:24 AM||||Don't forget to check out the cat converter.||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||09-28-1999||09:20 AM||||there are tests for the coil to check resistance, but they usually don't help. especially in this kind of problem. No the ECM will not set codes for coils tho coil problems may set other false codes.<P>check fuel pressure on it. low pressure will cause a problem even if the injector is new. The new injector could be screwy. <P>the TPS could have a bad spot in it. The TPS has moving parts and does were out. since the engine spends allot of time in that range its posible the resistor is worn out in that range. If the TPS is funky the ECM doesn't know for sure where the pedal is and sets wrong injector timing.<P>the map sensor could be bad, have a dirty conection, or a plugged/damaged vacuum line. but I think you'd see problems with it in more than just a narrow range.<P>If you had an ECM scanner you could watch most of what's going on in the DIS motor in real time. then you could likely see what sensor is hosed, if it's a sensor. that would at least narrow it down really quick.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Eddie||09-28-1999||06:54 PM||||Hay thanks guy,s it was the 3 plug wire it was not all yhe way on . Also no more red manifold<P>	Eddie||||reg||6
